id: E211
category: platform_compat
keywords: pthread_getaffinity_np pthread_setaffinity_np musl libc affinity thread
symptoms:
  - compile error: "undeclared identifier 'pthread_getaffinity_np'"
  - compile error: "undeclared identifier 'pthread_setaffinity_np'"
  - compile error: "did you mean 'sched_setaffinity'"
diagnosis:
  - software uses pthread affinity extensions (glibc-specific)
  - musl libc does not implement pthread_getaffinity_np/pthread_setaffinity_np
  - OpenHarmony uses musl libc
root_cause: musl libc lacks glibc pthread affinity extensions
solutions:
  - replace pthread_getaffinity_np with sched_getaffinity(0, ...)
  - replace pthread_setaffinity_np with sched_setaffinity(0, ...)
  - pid=0 means current thread/process
  - ensure cpu_set_t type is available via sched.h
examples:
  - software: OpenImageDenoise
    file: core/thread.cpp
    patch: 0002-core-thread.cpp.patch
notes: |
  musl libc provides standard POSIX functions but lacks glibc extensions.
  sched_getaffinity/sched_setaffinity are standard POSIX and work on musl.
  The first argument (pid_t pid) set to 0 means the calling thread/process.
affected_software:
  - OpenImageDenoise
  - TBB (potential)
  - OpenMPI (potential)
  - any software using pthread affinity APIs
